setupX11(){
while true
do
echo "
Newer versions of Ubuntu, which I use, have changed the default windowing system to wayland. I have found that qpdfview give error messages under weyland. Although the program still works, you can eliminate the error messages by changing the windowing system back to X11.

You may toggle your windowing system under Ubuntu by:
    1.  Click on the power 0n/Off button at top right to show its menu
    2.  Choose Settings/Users
    3.  Disable automatic login
    4.  Logout, then login
    5.  Press a key to have the screen ask for you password.
    6.  At this point there will be a small settings icon in the lower right.
    7.  Click on the icon.
    8.  Two clickable choices are presented for use during this log-in session.
       	   Ubuntu
	   Ubuntu on X.org
    9.  Click on 'Ubuntu' to use wayland or
   10.  Click on 'Ubuntu on X.org' to use X11

 To return to the previous menu enter 'q'. 

   q) Return to previous menu."

   read click

     case "$click" in

        q) return;;
	*) echo "Choice not recognized."
	   echo "Enter q to return to the previous menu.";;
     esac
done
}